    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nanimate\n\n### Description\n\nI am currently running neovim 0.9.0 and `mini.nvim` at commit `a7c3753`. When I enable the `animate` module with `scrolloff` enabled (mine is set to 8) I experience really erratic animations and the cursor seems to frequently jump upwards when trying to scroll down.\r\n\r\nHere is the minimal config I created to reproduce this issue:\r\n```lua\r\n-- Minimal config based on the example in folke/noice.nvim to prevent it from using existing lazy plugins\r\n-- https://github.com/folke/noice.nvim/wiki/Minimal-%60init.lua%60-to-Reproduce-an-Issue\r\nlocal root = vim.fn.fnamemodify(\"./nvim-repro\", \":p\")\r\n\r\n-- set stdpaths to use .repro\r\nfor _, name in ipairs({ \"config\", \"data\", \"state\", \"cache\" }) do\r\n   vim.env[(\"XDG_%s_HOME\"):format(name:upper())] = root .. \"/\" .. name\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- bootstrap lazy\r\nlocal lazypath = root .. \"/plugins/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n   vim.fn.system({\r\n      \"git\",\r\n      \"clone\",\r\n      \"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n      \"--single-branch\",\r\n      \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n      lazypath,\r\n   })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\n-- install plugins\r\nlocal plugins = {\r\n   \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\r\n   -- pinning the commit to the one where I experienced the issue\r\n   commit = \"a7c3753\",\r\n   config = function()\r\n      require(\"mini.animate\").setup({})\r\n   end,\r\n}\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup(plugins, {\r\n   root = root .. \"/plugins\",\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.opt.scrolloff = 8\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run neovim with the minimal config provided above: `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Open a file with enough lines that you can scroll\r\n3. Attempt to scroll up and down in the file\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nScrolling should move up and down normally without stuttering or moving in the wrong direction\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nWith no mini plugin and `scrolloff` set, this is what it looks like\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.opt.scrolloff = 8\r\n```\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/15240739/230755465-3ea9b2a1-c3ba-4601-a0ca-b63e4464ef40.mp4\r\n\r\nWith these configs, this is what it looks like when I try to scroll down.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.animate\").setup({})\r\nvim.opt.scrolloff = 8\r\n```\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/15240739/230755161-405c41b9-7f7c-470d-bee5-0abffab36c14.mp4\r\n\r\nAnd this is what it looks like when I try to scroll up\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/15240739/230755172-4e9557ec-0432-452d-8432-43fb5376f01f.mp4\r\n\r\nWhen I get rid of `scrolloff` it does let me scroll without jumping around (albeit really slowly but maybe I can change that with configuration?).\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.animate\").setup({})\r\n```\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/15240739/230755238-d374f081-2d4c-4f7d-a2d3-48f95d6a6d18.mp4\r\n\r\nIf I disable `scroll` in the animate module then the scrolling goes back to normal and looks like the first video\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.animate\").setup({\r\n   scroll = { enable = false },\r\n})\r\nvim.opt.scrolloff = 8\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n",
