            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I don't seem to see any scroll animation in that video, maybe you are mistaking where I am resetting my finger on the mouse's scroll wheel? \r\n\r\nAll of those videos were made using that minimal config, and that video had just `scrolloff` set and mini disabled in `lazy.nvim`, so the only plugin that would have been loaded was lazy. I also just went ahead and reproduced the issue with that minimal config on my macbook and iterm2, so I don't believe this is a terminal-specific issue either (the initial report is on windows terminal and wsl2 ubuntu).",
