            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I don't seem to see any scroll animation in that video, maybe you are mistaking where I am resetting my finger on the mouse's scroll wheel?\r\n> \r\n> All of those videos were made using that minimal config, and that video had just `scrolloff` set and mini disabled in `lazy.nvim`, so the only plugin that would have been loaded was lazy. I also just went ahead and reproduced the issue with that minimal config on my macbook and iterm2, so I don't believe this is a terminal-specific issue either (the initial report is on windows terminal and wsl2 ubuntu).\r\n\r\nHow do you scroll? I assumed you used something like `<C-d>` or `<C-f>`. Do you have this issue when you use mouse wheel to scroll? If yes, then this a limitation of async nature of this scroll (see [here in help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a7c375312edba618d7abc7c6129c53c512cca9d7/doc/mini-animate.txt#L277-L282)). Also try `set mousescroll=1` and scroll aggressively (many wheel turns per second) or `set mousescroll=30` and move wheel once.",
