            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ah I see. I do typically use those keymaps but these clips are from me using the mouse wheel. I will still rarely use the mouse and noticed it when I first tried after installing the plugin. If it's already a documented issue then that should be fine. Because the README had notes about scrolling (like using neovim 0.9.0) I was expecting that kind of note to be included in there as well, my apologies I should have probably dug into the help doc a little more. I was hoping to find a way to make the animations work for the keymaps but disable them for the mouse but it seems like that wouldn't be possible or make much sense from a logic point of view since both are scrolling, so maybe I'll just try to avoid the mouse for now.",
